WHAT DID NOT COMPLETE, AND WHY THIS LOG SAYS SO RATHER THAN HIDING IT
  Turn 1's LLM reply produced no visible tutor caption: state went
  thinking -> listening with no caption, no `error` message, and no
  `llm_pipeline_failed`/`llm_tools_unsupported` metric — the turn ran to
  completion, it just generated no text. The session then never heard a
  second learner utterance ("Guarda la palabra cigarra") for the rest of
  its life and ended on the normal 90s idle timeout.
  This is NOT the STT/LLM-contention regression this task was scoped to
  (STT itself is proven fast and correct above, in isolation, in the
  regression log's post-fix verification, and again here). It is also
  not new: the same "turn 1 completes silently, no caption" shape is
  visible in docs/evidence/browser-tutor-slice2-3-2026-09-05.log's own
  turn 1 (before any change in this task), so it predates this fix.
  Root cause not investigated here — out of scope for the STT regression
  this document is about, and outside the files this task's ownership
  ceiling covers (the WebLLM engine plumbing itself, worker.ts, is in
  scope, but no error surfaced there to chase; the audio-capture chain
  that would need checking next, apps/client/src/platform/audio-adapter.ts,
  is not owned by this task). Flagged for a follow-up, not silently
  shipped as passing.

